This file gathers and re-exports the primitive-recursive interval arithmetic for the universal domain: the basic encoding, combination, and difference operations together with their presentation lemmas, membership in a decoded list of rational pairs, primitive recursiveness of the pair-combination operation and the decoding of that operation, primitive recursiveness of the combination code, membership in a decoded combination and in a combination of interval lists, the set-level correctness of combination, the presentation of a folded single difference, of subtracting a whole list from one interval, and of subtracting two lists, primitive recursiveness of the one-interval, single-list, fold-step, whole-list, and two-list difference codes, primitive recursiveness of the nonemptiness operation and the criterion that it equals one, primitive recursiveness of the nonemptiness character, the bound of that character by one, and the criterion that it equals one, the nonemptiness and subset criteria for decoded presentations, and the recursive decidability of nonemptiness, subset, and equality of presented intervals.
